{
 "_comment": "METRICS 6.9, written by hand and checked by spec/tools/intelligence.py. `grades` resolve against the fixture price table `table`; `effort` is the normalized effort token (EXECUTION-MODES) or absent. `windows` give engine responses (with `reasoning`, `effort`, `provider`) and agents (with `effort`) as engine-cases.json does; a query's `sources` restricts both to an orb's set. `shown` is the intelligence rounded half away from zero; null when nothing generated in the window. `agentWindows` (METRICS 6.9, Agent intelligence) have the shape of `windows` with every case's agents in each query's `agents`: `form` live / resting / none, `intelligence` (the live value, or the grade at rest; null for none), `shown`, the agent's own `liveThinking` and `thinkingShare`, and `grade` (its current model, effort and latest named provider; null without a model); `expect` is the whole set's, which the agents' sums add up to.",
